# Focused run of the 24 behaviour cases this branch adds to tests/fm-backlog-atomicity.test.sh (exit=0)
ok - an interrupt before the kill keeps every record for a rerun
ok - completion marks a pending close whose worker could not be proved stopped, and recovery honours it
ok - a herdr refusal marks its pending close, and recovery honours it
ok - a refusal before the kill leaves its pending close unconfirmed, and replay honours it
ok - an interrupt after a proven kill still replays its close
ok - no automatic path retires a record no backend can answer for
ok - retirement requires exact record identities and refuses wildcards
ok - a retirement carries who asserted it and when, and is consumed by the cleanup it authorizes
ok - a retirement leaves work on disk byte-untouched and names what remains
ok - only the named override flag retires a record whose runtime refused, and it is recorded
ok - an interrupt during a retirement retires nothing and leaves no authorization
ok - a refusal other than the work gate stops the retirement
ok - a cleanup that failed partway is reported as partial, not as a no-op
ok - a backlog row that cannot be read refuses the retirement instead of losing the record
ok - a captain-held row is retained with its deliverable, not closed as done
ok - a manual-backlog home retires its record and its backlog is left as the operator keeps it
ok - a record-only retirement takes its pending close with it
ok - a retirement records the record, its author, the time and the override durably
ok - a retirement that cannot record its author retires nothing
ok - a retirement keeps its record when the pending close cannot be cleared
ok - a retirement leaves a close session start can finish
ok - the retirement command's help states the condition it is for
ok - session start refuses to replay a close whose worker was never proved stopped
ok - session start still finishes an ordinary interrupted cleanup
